[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627549180","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102243#issuecomment-2627549180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102243","id":2627549180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cnTf8","user":{"login":"atirutw","id":25323231,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MzIzMjMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25323231?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw","html_url":"https://github.com/atirutw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atirutw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T14:57:33Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T14:57:33Z","body":"Would this help with baking large, high quality lightmaps? I wonder if it could be enabled automatically when there's not enough VRAM for a bake.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627549180/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627583284","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102243#issuecomment-2627583284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102243","id":2627583284,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cnb00","user":{"login":"badsectoracula","id":20316467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T15:12:37Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T15:12:37Z","body":"> Would this help with baking large, high quality lightmaps?\r\n\r\nWell, it would help baking larger and more detailed lightmaps, as long as a single lightmap slice (texture array layer) can fit into VRAM together with all the other stuff the lightmapper needs in the VRAM. Most importantly the lightmapper still needs to create a full texture array (i.e. all slices) to store albedo and emissive textures and it still duplicates all geometry into VRAM. These are needed for shadows and indirect lighting, so i can't think of a way to avoid them (at least not without fundamentally changing how the lightmapper works :-P).\r\n\r\n> I wonder if it could be enabled automatically when there's not enough VRAM for a bake.\r\n\r\nThis is something i looked into but AFAICT there is no portable and reliable way to obtain the available VRAM.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627583284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627625729","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102243#issuecomment-2627625729","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102243","id":2627625729,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cnmMB","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T15:31:05Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T15:31:05Z","body":"> Currently enabling the low VRAM mode is done via a new property in the `LightmapGI` node. There was some discussion in a recent rendering meeting about not adding a new property for this but instead piggybacking on `use_texture_for_bounces` and assume low VRAM is desired if it is `false` since the low VRAM mode ignores the lightmap texture (as it isn't fully available in VRAM anyway). Personally i'm not a fan of this as it is about something separate and i'd prefer more explicit control, but at the end i do not hold strong opinions either way - the important is getting it in the engine so that people with low VRAM can use it.\r\n\r\nI'd say this should be an editor setting, as not all users working on the same project will have the same amount of VRAM available on their GPU.\r\n\r\n> This is something i looked into but AFAICT there is no portable and reliable way to obtain the available VRAM.\r\n\r\nVulkan/Direct3D 12/Metal make this possible in a portable way, but not OpenGL. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4871.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627625729/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627668845","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102243#issuecomment-2627668845","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102243","id":2627668845,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cnwtt","user":{"login":"SpockBauru","id":67930504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3OTMwNTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67930504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru","html_url":"https://github.com/SpockBauru","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpockBauru/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T15:51:18Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T16:30:49Z","body":"Came from #101391 and tested the [hundred trees MRP](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17580558/shadowmask_test_2.zip) with the Windows Artifact.\r\n\r\nEnabled the `Low VRAM Mode`  with everything else at the default settings.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/227657b1-86a6-4de9-9efd-3ac60384a99c)\r\n\r\nThe setting does not solve #101391, it still crashes Godot every time on the same spot.\r\n\r\nMy system:\r\n```\r\nGodot v4.4.beta.gh-102243 [f8f03f17c] (windows artifact of this PR, 15dbf42)\r\nWindows 11 23H2 (did not updated to 24H2 yet)\r\nNVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 - 12GB variant - Driver 566.14\r\n12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-12700KF (20 threads)\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627668845/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628024563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102243#issuecomment-2628024563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102243","id":2628024563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cpHjz","user":{"login":"badsectoracula","id":20316467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T18:18:34Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T18:18:34Z","body":"> Enabled the `Low VRAM Mode` with everything else at the default settings.\r\n> The setting does not solve #101391, it still crashes Godot every time on the same spot.\r\n\r\nYeah this PR wouldn't help because that MRP generates a lightmap array texture with a single 8192x8192 entry, so it does essentially the same work and uses the same VRAM as without enabling low VRAM mode. AFAICT the reason is the lightmap coordinates for a mesh cannot fit.\r\n\r\nTry to set the texture scale to 0.95 (which shouldn't make much of a visual difference in this case as the generated lightmap is only using half the allocated space and the blocking mesh is only a tiny bit larger than what would fit in 4096x4096) and maximum texture size to 4096. This should generate a lightmap with two 4096x4096 array slices.\r\n\r\nAs i wrote in the PR description, for this PR to make a difference you need to ensure that there will be multiple lightmap array slices - the default values wont cut it because they try to minimize the number of slices and maximize slice resolution, based on the assumption that there will be enough VRAM (and a fast enough GPU to avoid timeout issues).\r\n\r\nTo make the most of this PR you'd need to:\r\n\r\n1. Use a smaller maximum texture size like 2048 or 4096\r\n2. Avoid too large meshes _or_ use smaller lightmap scaling values for large meshes\r\n3. In general ensure there are multiple lightmap array slices\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628024563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628256317","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102243#issuecomment-2628256317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102243","id":2628256317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cqAI9","user":{"login":"solitaryurt","id":95145240,"node_id":"U_kgDOBavNGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95145240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt","html_url":"https://github.com/solitaryurt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solitaryurt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T19:51:03Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T19:51:03Z","body":"Would this also help with large `supersampling_factor` values?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628256317/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628518326","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102243#issuecomment-2628518326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102243","id":2628518326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6crAG2","user":{"login":"badsectoracula","id":20316467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T22:40:36Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T22:40:36Z","body":"> Would this also help with large `supersampling_factor` values?\r\n\r\nYes, it'd be the same as if using a large texture scale. For example in the modified TPS demo setting texture scale to 1.5 *or* supersampling factor to 3 with a texture scale of 0.5 needs about 24GB of VRAM in normal mode and about 8GB of VRAM in low VRAM mode.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628518326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628979691","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102243#issuecomment-2628979691","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102243","id":2628979691,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cswvr","user":{"login":"jcostello","id":1168582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjg1ODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1168582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello","html_url":"https://github.com/jcostello","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T14:43:43Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T14:43:43Z","body":"This works like a charm. It saves a lot of VRAM in the baking process","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628979691/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]